= Incentive — Technical =

In a simple choice model, an incentive changes payoffs or constraints so that <pre>argmax_a U(a)</pre> may change. In contract and mechanism models the design problem is not merely to increase a payoff, but to alter strategic behavior while respecting information, participation, risk, and feasibility constraints.

== Modeling cautions ==
* incentive ≠ reward only
* stated incentive ≠ actual behavioral effect
* incentive alignment ≠ identical interests

